{"id":"word:hebrew:H3898","type":"word","title":"לָחַם","subtitle":"H3898 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to feed on ; figuratively, to consume ; by implication, to battle (as destruction)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to לָחַם (H3898) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 177 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"לָחַם (lâcham) means to feed on ; figuratively, to consume ; by implication, to battle (as destruction) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 10 1."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"לָחַם","transliteration":"lâcham","pronunciation":"law-kham'","strong":"H3898","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3898","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יִּלָּ֖חֶם","לְ/הִלָּחֵ֖ם","וַ/יִּֽלָּחֲמ֖וּ","לְ/הִלָּחֵ֣ם","וַ/יִּלָּ֣חֶם"],"morphs":[["HR/VNc",42],["HC/VNw3ms",20],["HVNp3ms",16],["HC/VNw3mp",15],["HVNrmpa",8],["HVNp3cp",7],["HVNrmsa",7],["HVNi2mp",5],["HC/VNq3ms",5],["HC/VNq3cp",5]]},"definitions":{"short":"to feed on ; figuratively, to consume ; by implication, to battle (as destruction)","usage":"devour, eat, × ever, fight(-ing), overcome, prevail, (make) war(-ring).","full":"H3898. lacham I. [ לָחַם ] 171 verb fight, do battle (Late Hebrew Hithpa`el; ואלתחם MI 11.15.19 perhaps = order the battle , compare Nö ZMG xl. 1886, 721 ; Arabic fit close together , so Late Hebrew לחם Pi`el, Syriac Pa`el unite , fit also threaten ; Gerber Verb. Denom. 59 thinks verb in Hebrew denominative from מִלְחָמָה battle-line , but dubious); — Qal (poetry) only Imperative masculine singular and Participle active — fight, do battle with, rare, only Psalms, apparently later usage: &#8212; אֶתלֹֿחֲמָ֑י לְחַם Psa 35:1 do battle with those battling with me (dubious whether את is accusative sign compare preposition with , compare Ol; || אֶתיְֿרִיבַי רִיבָה ); לִי לֹחֲמִים 56:3 doing battle against me ; לֹחֵם 56:2 as substantive fighter. Niph`al 167 Perfect נִלְחַם Judg 9:17 +, וְנִלְחַמְתָּ֫ 11:8 ; 1Sam 15:18 , וְנִלְחַמְנוּ Deut 1:41 consecutive, etc.; Imperfect יִלָּהֵם Exod 14:14 ; Deut 1:30 ; לָ֑נוּ יִלָּ֫חֶם Neh 4:14 , וַיִּלָּ֫חֶם Exod 17:8 19t.; 3 feminine singular תִּלָּחֵם Zech 14:14 ; 3 masculine plural תִּיִּלָּֽחֲמוּ Judg 1:5 13 t.; suffix וַיִּלָּֽחֲמוּנִי Psa 109:3 ; 2 masculine plural תִּלָּֽחֲמוּ 1Kin 22:31 4 t.; תִּלָּֽחֲמוּן 12:24 .; etc.; Imperative הִלָּחֵם Exod 17:9 ; 1Sam 18:17 ; בּוֺ הִלָּ֫חֶם Judg 9:38 ; plural הִלָּֽחֲמוּ 2Kin 10:3 ; Neh 4:8 ; Infinitive absolute נִלְחֹם Judg 11:25 ; construct הִלָּחֵם 1:9 35 t.; בּוֺ הִלָּ֫חֶם etc., Num 22:11 6 t.; suffix הִלָּחֲמוֺ 2Kin 8:29 3 t.; Participle נִלְחָם Exod 14:24 10 t.; plural נִלְחָמִים Josh 10:25 10 t. (but 1Sam 31:1 read rather נִלְחֲמוּ , so || 1Chr 10:1 We Klo Bu, compare Dr); — engage in battle (reciprocal), sometimes wage war ( Josh 10:5 ; Judg 11:5 ; 1Kin 14:19 ; 22:46 ; 2Kin 6:8 ; 14:28 etc.), often with בְּ of enemy (60 t.) Exod 1:10 ; 17:9-10 , Num 21:23 , 26 ; 22:11 (all E), Judg 11:8 , 25 ; 1Sam 15:18 ; 2Sam 8:10 + (49 t.); less often with בְּ of city attacked or besieged Judg 9:45 ; 1Sam 23:1 ; 2Sam 12:26-27 , 29 ; Isa 20:1 ; Josh 10:31 (D), 1Kin 20:1 ; Neh 4:2 ; of tower Judges 1:52; followed by בְּאַרְצִי Judg 11:12 ; also with עִם of enemy (26 t.): 5:20 ; 11:4-5 , 20 ; Josh 11:5 (JE), 1Sam 13:5 ; 17:19 , also 17:32-33 , (of single combat), Deut 20:4 ; Josh 9:2 (both D), 2Kin 13:12 ; 14:15 ; 2Chr 11:1 ; 17:10 ; 27:5 ; Dan 10:20 ; 11:11 +; with עִם of city Josh 10:29 (D), 19:47 (JE); c אֶתֿ = with , of enemy, 24:8 (E), 1Sam 17:9 (single combat), Jer 21:5 ; 1Kin 20:23 ; 2Kin 19:9 = Isa 37:9 ; Jer 37:10 ; also Judg 12:4 ; 2Sam 11:17 ; 21:15 ; 1Kin 22:31 ; 2Kin 8:2 ; 9:15 ; Jer 21:4 ; 32:5 ; 33:5 ; 2Chr 18:30 ; 22:6 , and with אוֺתָם (= אִתָּם ) Josh 10:25 (D), 1Kin 20:25 (Kö Lgb. ii, 296 ); with עִל , against , of enemy only Jer 21:2 ; elsewhere (16 t.) of city: Josh 10:5 (JE), Isa 7:1 ; 2Kin 12:18 ; 19:8 = Isa 37:8 ; especially D and Je: Deut 20:10 , 19 ; Josh 10:34 , 36 , 38 (all D), Jer 32:24 , 29 ; 34:1 , 7 , 8 , 22 ; with אֶלֿ of enemy 1:19 ; 15:20 ; with suffix וַיִּלָּֽחֲמוּנִי Psa 109:3 and they have fought against me ; with יָ֑חַד i.e. fight together = with (against) one another 1Sam 17:10 ; absolute with accusative of congnate meaning with verb מִלְחָמוֺת fight battles 8:20 ; 18:17 ; 25:28 ; 2Chr 32:8 ; absolute elsewhere Judg 5:19 (twice in verse); 5:20 ; Deut 1:41 ; Zech 10:5 26t. + לְהִלָּחֵ֑ם עָלָיו וַיָּסֻרוּ 1Kin 22:32 ; with עַל for, in behalf of , Judg 9:17 ; 2Kin 10:3 ; Neh 4:8 ; with לְ = id ., Exod 14:14 (J), 14:25 (J; + בְּ of enemy), Deut 1:30 ; 3:22 ; 20:4 (+ עִם of enemy, see above), Josh 10:14 , 42 ; 23:3 , 10 (all D), Neh 4:14 לְהִלּ ׳יָכֹל be able to fight , with את of enemy 1Sam 17:9 , with בְּ of enemy Num 22:11 , = be successful in fighting , prevail against; so with עַל of city Isa 7:1 , and absolute 2Kin 16:5 (after עָל וַיָּצֻרוּ besiege ). II. [ לָחַם ] verb use as food, eat , poetic (so Thes Buhl, compare Frä 30 Guidi Della Sede 33 ; this would explain different between לֶחֶם and ; yet verb rare and chiefly late); &#8212; Qal Perfect 3plural לָֽחֲמוּ Prov 4:17 ; Imperfect 2masculine singular תִּלְחַם 23:6 , 1 singular אֶלְחַם Psa 141:4 ; Imperative masculine plural לַחֲמוּ Prov 9:5 ; Infinitive construct לְחוֺם 23:1 ; Passive participle plural construct לְחֻמֵי Deut 32:24 ; eat (mostly Proverbs), absolute Prov 23:1 ; followed by accusative of congnate meaning with verb לֶחֶם 4:17 ; 23:6 ; followed by בְּלַחְמִי 9:5 ; followed by בְּמַנְעַמֵּיהֶם Psa 141:4 eat of their dainties ; רֶשֶׁף לְחֻמֵי Deut 32:24 (poem) eaten up with the Fire-bolt , figurative of pestilence (Dr).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 10 1","keyReferences":["1Chr 10 1","1Chr 18 10","1Chr 19 17","1Kgs 12 21","1Kgs 12 24","1Kgs 14 19","1Kgs 20 1","1Kgs 20 23"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"co